      <body>
         <head>The knife-grinder's budget of pictures &amp; poetry, for boys and girls</head>
         <author>Unknown</author>
         <p rend="color(#000000)">{{GUTENBERG_LICENSE}}</p>
         <p rend="start color(#000000)">en-gutenberg-odts/t/The knife-grinders budget of pictures &amp; poetry, for boys and girls.54530.odt</p>
         <head>The Knife Grinder’s Budget</head>
         <p>The Knife Grinder’s Budget</p>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>The knife-grinder's budget of pictures &amp; poetry, for boys and girls</head>
            <lg>
               <l>“Swing-up, my Lads!”</l>
               <l>The Drill-Sergeant cries,</l>
               <l>“And fix on the Fugle-man</l>
               <l>Each of your eyes.”</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">PRICE ONE PENNY.</p>
            <p rend="justify">FRONTISPIECE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">FRONTISPIECE</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE KNIFE-GRINDER.</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="bold">KNIFE-GRINDER</hi>’s</p>
            <p rend="justify">Budget</p>
            <p rend="justify">OF</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Pictures &amp; Poetry</hi>,</p>
            <p rend="justify">FOR</p>
            <p rend="justify">BOYS AND GIRLS.</p>
            <p rend="justify">OTLEY:</p>
            <p rend="justify">PRINTED BY WILLIAM WALKER.</p>
            <p rend="justify">1829.</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="bold">THE BUDGET</hi>
            </p>
            <p rend="justify">“Come buy my fine Apples,”</p>
            <lg>
               <l>“Come buy my fine Apples,”</l>
               <l>The old Woman cries,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>“You cannot have better</l>
               <l>For eating or pies.”</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">donkey</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The Huxter and Donkey</l>
               <l>  Are both on their legs:</l>
               <l/>
               <l>They’re going to market</l>
               <l>  For butter and eggs.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">barber</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The Barber, of all men,</l>
               <l>  Is most full of news,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>And ever detested</l>
               <l>  By long-bearded Jews.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">riding</p>
            <lg>
               <l>“Well, Richard, you’re mounted</l>
               <l>  Again, I declare!”</l>
               <l/>
               <l>“Yes, riding is better</l>
               <l>  Than walking, by far!”</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">goat</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The Goat on the crag</l>
               <l>  You see fast asleep;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>From whence he can leap,</l>
               <l>  Tho’ it’s ever so steep.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">child_cat</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The Child and Miss Pussy</l>
               <l>  Do play very nice;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>But Pussy had much rather</l>
               <l>  Play with some mice.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">lamp-lighter</p>
            <lg>
               <l>“Be quick as a Lamp-lighter!”</l>
               <l>  Sometimes we say:</l>
               <l/>
               <l>Here’s one upon duty</l>
               <l>  Fast tripping away.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">dog</p>
            <lg>
               <l>O, Keeper! thy visage</l>
               <l>  Is dreadful indeed!</l>
               <l/>
               <l>Thy presence I’ll flee</l>
               <l>  With all possible speed.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">butcher_calf</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Here comes for the Butcher</l>
               <l>  A fine lusty Calf,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>For the killing of which</l>
               <l>  He perhaps will get half.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">potato_farm</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Potatoes are useful,</l>
               <l>  If they be but good:</l>
               <l/>
               <l>The ground must be till’d,</l>
               <l>  Or we cannot have food.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">hound</p>
            <lg>
               <l>That Hound, I dare say,</l>
               <l>  Won’t like the Boy’s whip;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>Could he break the cord,</l>
               <l>  He would give him the slip.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">boot-jack</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Poor Jack! I’m afraid</l>
               <l>  That thy bum will be sore:</l>
               <l/>
               <l>That footmen were boot-jacks</l>
               <l>  I ne’er knew before.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">chair_repair</p>
            <lg>
               <l>You here see a poor man</l>
               <l>  Repairing a chair;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>He sits on the ground,</l>
               <l>  Quite expos’d to the air.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">sailor</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Silk, Cotton, and Sugar,</l>
               <l>  And Coffee, and Tea,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>Are fetch’d by the sailors</l>
               <l>  Across the great sea.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">Matilda_tray</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Poor Tray seems inclin’d</l>
               <l>  With Matilda to dine:</l>
               <l/>
               <l>He wants but the meat,—</l>
               <l>  He would leave her the wine.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">rabbit_pie</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Come buy my fat Rabbits,</l>
               <l>  Come, Ladies, and buy;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>With mutton they make</l>
               <l>  A most excellent pie.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">hen</p>
            <lg>
               <l>When the Hen calls her Chickens,</l>
               <l>  They follow straight-way;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>So Children should always</l>
               <l>  Their Parents obey.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">laundress</p>
            <lg>
               <l>You see the old Laundress</l>
               <l>  At work in her drills;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>But I fear she’s too old</l>
               <l>  To crimp you your frills.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">sweeping_brush</p>
            <lg>
               <l>“Buy a good sweeping-brush,—</l>
               <l>  Hand-brushes buy,—</l>
               <l/>
               <l>I’ll sell you cheap brushes,”—</l>
               <l>  The old man doth cry.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">lady</p>
            <lg>
               <l>This Lady of pleasure</l>
               <l>  Is taking fresh air;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>Which may do very well,</l>
               <l>  If the weather keep fair.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">ned</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Poor Ned, I’m afraid,</l>
               <l>  Cannot meet with his horse;</l>
               <l/>
               <l>He seems quite distracted</l>
               <l>  At so great a loss.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">girl_swinging</p>
            <lg>
               <l>The Girl you see swinging,</l>
               <l>  If the band only break,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>Will be in great danger</l>
               <l>  Of breaking her neck.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">A Bull-baiting now</p>
            <lg>
               <l>A Bull-baiting now</l>
               <l>Puts an end to my book:</l>
               <l/>
               <l>The scene is so cruel,</l>
               <l>I can scarce bear to look.</l>
               <l/>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">W. Walker, Printer, Otley.</hi>
            </p>
            <p rend="justify">The Knife Grinder’s Budget</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Old Billy, poor man!</l>
               <l>Is depriv’d of his sight,</l>
               <l>But still with his music</l>
               <l>Produces delight.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">PRICE ONE PENNY.</p>
            <p rend="justify">Transcriber’s Note: Punctuation has been standardized.</p>
         </div>
      </body>
